  {
    "path": "openai-proof-research/frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/new-twenty-2026-10-31/expanded-corpus-r40/PROOF-ATTEMPTS.md",
    "excerpt": "openai-proof-research/frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/new-twenty-2026-10-31/expanded-corpus-r40/PROOF-ATTEMPTS.md:5:Primary manuscript 2008.11448, Definitions 2\u20133 and Section 7.2, Conjecture 3, actually read. A strategy is a partition of S_n into n labelled parts. For a part C_h, magneticity of position i for target k is the cardinality of {\u03c3\u2208C_h:\u03c3(i)=k}; intensity is the maximum over positions. Field is the sum of intensities over h,k. Optimality means maximum field, not merely asymptotic order. Latin strategies use a Latin-square row with maximum agreements; arbitrary tie choices are expressly allowed in the paragraph preceding the conjecture. The published Wiley URL returned403; no retry. Web-indexed publisher text agrees, but this is not an independently downloaded published-body audit."
  },
